Goldeneye-Native
================

Scope of the MIT licence in LICENSE
-----------------------------------

The MIT licence covers the original work in this repository: the platform layer
under getv/port/ (excluding the fetched third-party sources listed below), the
build scripts, the tooling under tools/, and the documentation.

It does not and cannot cover the following, which are not ours to license.

Decompiled game source
----------------------

The game's C source under vendor/ge-decomp/ comes from the n64decomp/007
decompilation project, which publishes no licence file. Its libultra sources
carry SGI proprietary headers. That is upstream's situation and is not resolved
by this repository. The decompilation is not distributed here; it is fetched
separately.

Third-party port sources
------------------------

Several files in the platform layer derive from sm64ex, which itself derives
its Fast3D implementation from Emill/n64-fast3d-engine. sm64ex ships no root
licence, and the Fast3D notice it reproduces prohibits binary redistribution.
GitHub classifies the upstream repository as NOASSERTION.

Because that situation is unresolved, those files are not distributed here.
tools/fetch-thirdparty.sh retrieves them from upstream at a pinned commit and
applies our changes as a patch series. See docs/THIRD_PARTY.md and
docs/LICENSING.md.

Game data
---------

No ROM, no extracted assets, no textures, no audio, no level data, and no
game-derived material of any kind is included in this repository or in its
history. Building requires a copy of the game that you own. See README.md.

